d country sees a high number of deadly encounters.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea proposes military talks with North again</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e7d2ca9004b7c468c617985c91161254be8c9bed750db79b33ed68168037f49</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:38:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T07:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-proposes-military-talks-with-north-again/a-79739208--5b2219c381d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-proposes-military-talks-with-north-again/a-79739208?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">South Korea is attempting to mutually determine the land border with North Korea amid military incidents and escalating tensions.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Taiwan braces as El Nino-supercharged Typhoon Champi approaches island</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4654f34ca31d09c80d26bda615a2390883d02d4d83b09b22ccafe538d97759ff</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:38:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T06:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/taiwan-braces-as-el-nino-supercharged-typhoon-champi-approaches-island/a-79738819--5f04cbf55cee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/taiwan-braces-as-el-nino-supercharged-typhoon-champi-approaches-island/a-79738819?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">One person has died and thousands have been evacuated as Taiwan prepares for a possible direct hit. Though no longer a "super" typhoon, Champi is still packing winds of nearly 200 kmh and will bring torrential rain.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Protesters march to Election Commission demanding CEC Gyanesh Kumar's resignation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:acf7c4a4d8e2ed901e0e43675af3d708cf1d359afc9816ef9b168d1c6ecd0551</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:38:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T04:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-protesters-march-to-election-commission-demanding-cec-gyanesh-kumar-s-resignation/live-79738437--359ae058742e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-protesters-march-to-election-commission-demanding-cec-gyanesh-kumar-s-resignation/live-79738437?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A coalition of students, farmers and civil society groups have joined calls for Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar's resignation over India's voter roll revision exercise. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Tibet earthquake kills at least 16 people, injures dozens: state media</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:460f01e871c09d9979b06951b32d4987d17d79416e5e8fee6c3e654c6c63fdd6</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T23:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tibet-earthquake-kills-at-least-16-people-injures-dozens-state-media/a-79738117--804f662ec522.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tibet-earthquake-kills-at-least-16-people-injures-dozens-state-media/a-79738117?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A powerful magnitude 7 earthquake has struck Tibet in southwestern China, official media reported. Chinese state TV said it's the strongest quake to hit the remote Himalayan region in five years.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Is Iran ready for another major US attack after midterm elections?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2990e6af897ff6d89bea2baf498b9969500cd8a738a1089ebe69e7e6a5962cb8</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T14:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-iran-ready-for-another-major-us-attack-after-midterm-elections/a-79734082--65d965ab6d67.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-iran-ready-for-another-major-us-attack-after-midterm-elections/a-79734082?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iranian officials say the goal is to keep the regime in power and threaten enough regional costs to make a prolonged campaign unattractive. US media reports indicate that Trump is considering strikes after the midterms.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Is EU putting profits over human rights in Vietnam?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca3e64cb51a14ee7379b57c010a50a6d4c85766ddf20c0ba61ac9fd23d9dfe33</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T14:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-eu-putting-profits-over-human-rights-in-vietnam/a-79732812--0a31793443b5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-eu-putting-profits-over-human-rights-in-vietnam/a-79732812?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU and Vietnam are deepening economic and diplomatic ties, but closer cooperation raises concerns about whether Brussels is doing enough to address Hanoi's human rights record, labor standards and trade imbalances.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Gandhi's nephew forced to pull protest photos</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:36b8c680b08b682523982c108e0415c6589d338c1f6e15199e94e6f26c04ceff</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T12:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-gandhi-s-nephew-forced-to-pull-protest-photos/live-79727462--8042d9d73860.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-gandhi-s-nephew-forced-to-pull-protest-photos/live-79727462?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The requested removal of "objectionable" photos from a cultural center took place in state run by Modi's BJP.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran's Balochistan border region sees growing unrest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ddaa4673530cb9ef00d38aafd80a9f3eada17c1ba1d1bfda094d2a84060260c5</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T11:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-s-balochistan-border-region-sees-growing-unrest/a-79716399--7cda0ee86ea1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-s-balochistan-border-region-sees-growing-unrest/a-79716399?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Violence is on the rise in Iran's border region with Afghanistan and Pakistan. The Iran war could shift the strategic balance for militant groups operating in the area.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan-Taliban conflict: How India could benefit from shifting regional dynamics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a44371974eaa50194551865309a78403d2d7566a61ec74185f536a3b45bc3fc1</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T10:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-taliban-conflict-how-india-could-benefit-from-shifting-regional-dynamics/a-79721426--f7ab516276cd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-taliban-conflict-how-india-could-benefit-from-shifting-regional-dynamics/a-79721426?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Pakistan's influence in Afghanistan comes under strain, India is rebuilding ties with the Taliban in Kabul. Can New Delhi turn this diplomatic opening into lasting strategic gains?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>North Korean workers treated as 'slaves' at Russian drone factory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb241807f107024ba74b3825f2aa8948b0e8328bc317d645f513c3383d45ef0b</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T17:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korean-workers-treated-as-slaves-at-russian-drone-factory/a-79710877--83771c04f78a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korean-workers-treated-as-slaves-at-russian-drone-factory/a-79710877?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new report reveals the plight of North Korean workers at a drone factory in Russia. It also raised concerns that Pyongyang could gain hands-on knowledge of advanced weapons systems through the workers it sends there.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Who are the women powering India's youth-led 'Cockroach' protests?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e6a9c40dd754703cd229bef7547028e2825ba7893d4758eaa415a4ea4bd45cd7</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-are-the-women-powering-india-s-youth-led-cockroach-protests/a-79709824--e78a361757e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-are-the-women-powering-india-s-youth-led-cockroach-protests/a-79709824?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Facing online harassment and police detentions, women are taking to the streets of Indian cities in large numbers for the youth-led "Cockroach" protests. Amid a large-scale crackdown, they refuse to be seen as victims.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Brutal, revolutionary empire builder: Genghis Khan's legacy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60a6a61174d241e9be2370cee6bcba64de1ea54653965ea96e3c4c51802b9b54</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T08:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brutal-revolutionary-empire-builder-genghis-khan-s-legacy/a-79697112--675146225486.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brutal-revolutionary-empire-builder-genghis-khan-s-legacy/a-79697112?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Berlin is host to a major exhibition on the founder of the Mongol Empire and his successors. Here's how Genghis Khan disrupted the course of history.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Myanmar refugees find hope in Thailand's work program</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6f5fd316c9435e792a015903c08688e39ead8b329e23ca575e4ef277dcc70625</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/myanmar-refugees-find-hope-in-thailand-s-work-program/a-79697921--572ae4634b5b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/myanmar-refugees-find-hope-in-thailand-s-work-program/a-79697921?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A year ago, Thailand granted long-staying refugees from Myanmar the right to work legally. Refugees and rights groups welcome the move but say the program's first year has exposed significant shortcomings.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
